UID:c405f69a48ce7288@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260916T165049Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Needham Day - September 26
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the Maine Needham was first introduced in 1872 by 
 John Seavey\, owner of the confectionary Seavey’s Sweets\, which is rumo
 red to have been located in either Auburn or Portland at the time\; and\nW
 HEREAS\n\, named after a popular preacher of that era\, George C. Needham\
 , the Needham candy consists of a mashed potato center surrounded by cocon
 ut and chocolate\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, it is thought that Needhams gained pop
 ularity with home cooks during the Great Depression\, when Maine people wo
 uld use their extra potato harvest to make the treat\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Ne
 edhams have become synonymous with Maine\, and they help celebrate locally
  harvested Maine potatoes\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, today\, sweet shops and home 
 cooks around our state keep the beloved tradition of the Needham alive by 
 continuing to produce and perfect this iconic Maine treat for us to enjoy 
 and share with the world\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, on September 26\, 2026 the fou
 rth annual Maine Needham Festival will be held at the Maine Tasting Center
  in Wiscasset to celebrate the Needham and it’s great history in Maine\;
  and\nWHEREAS\n\, in accordance with 1 MRSA § 150-S\, the State of Maine 
 observes the last Saturday in September each year as Maine Needham Day\;\n
 NOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the
  State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim September 26\, 2026 as\nMaine Needham
  Day\nand I urge all citizens to recognize the Needham’s history and cel
 ebrate this delectable Maine treat.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\
 nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand 
 at Augusta this tenth day\nof September Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://ww
 w.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-09-maine-
 needham-day-september-26
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-maine-needham-day-september-26
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
