SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Standing Order: Standing Order Regarding Admi
 ninstrative Order JB-24-03 Pilot Program to Conditionally Authorize Law St
 udent Externs to Provide Public Defense Services
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE \nSUPREME JUDICIAL COURT \nSTANDING ORDER REGAR
 DING  \nADMINISTRATIVE ORDER JB-24-03 \nPILOT PROGRAM TO CONDITIONALLY AUT
 HORIZE  \nLAW STUDENT EXTERNS TO PROVIDE \nPUBLIC DEFENSE SERVICES \n \nEf
 fective: September 4\, 2026 \n \n On December 18\, 2024\, the Supreme Judi
 cial Court adopted \nAdministrative Order JB-24-03\, Pilot Program to Cond
 itionally Authorize Law \nStudent Externs to Provide Public Defense Servic
 es.  The order provides that it \nexpires on September 5\, 2026. \n \n The
  Court has not determined whether to adopt the program \npermanently.  The
 re are\, however\, students enrolled in externships for the fall \nsemeste
 r of 2026 who will be unable to participate in the externships if the \nor
 der is allowed to expire.  \n \n Because it will take time to determine wh
 ether the program will be made \npermanent\, but the Court does not wish t
 o prevent the currently enrolled \nstudents from participating in their ex
 ternships\, it is hereby ORDERED that the \neffective term of the pilot pr
 ogram established by Administrative Order JB-24-\n03 is extended through J
 anuary 15\, 2027.   \n \n The University of Maine School of Law and the or
 ganizations hosting \nstudent externs should not arrange for student exter
 ns for the spring semester \nof 2027 without first confirming that the pil
 ot program will remain in effect for \nthat semester. \n \n Dated: Septemb
 er 4\, 2026   For the Court: \n \n \n \n         /s/     \n        Valerie
  Stanfill \n        Chief Justice\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorder
 s/so-jb-24-03.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-jb-24-03.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:44a597a93c205705@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260914T124052Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Primary Care Plus (PCPlus) Quality Webinar: T
 otal Cost Index (TCI)
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Primary Care Plus (PCPlus) Quality Webinar: Total Cost 
 Index (TCI)\nPrimary Care Plus (PCPlus) Quality Webinar: Total Cost Index 
 (TCI)\nSep 26\, 2026\nWe invite PCPlus providers to a quality webinar seri
 es that educates providers and administrators on best practices related to
  quality measures in the PCPlus program. This series helps practices optim
 ize their performance and payment while aligning with industry best practi
 ces for population and patient health. MaineCare PCPlus quality measures c
 an be found on the\nPCPlus website\n.\nJoin us on September 28\, 2026 from
  12:00-1:00 PM for our next webinar. We are partnering with The Cutler Ins
 titute to learn more about the TCI measure and review the measure’s spec
 ifications. More information on the TCI measure can be found on the\nHealt
 h Partners Website\n.\nPlease register\nin advance for this meeting. After
  registering\, you will receive a confirmation email with information abou
 t joining the meeting.\nFor questions about PCPlus\, please contact us at\
 nPCP-Network-Services.DHHS@maine.gov\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/pr
 oviders/provider-bulletins/primary-care-plus-pcplus-quality-webinar-total-
 cost-index-tci-2026-09-14
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/primary-ca
 re-plus-pcplus-quality-webinar-total-cost-index-tci-2026-09-14
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
