UID:96966770dfad3fdf@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260910T205020Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce
  Waste Characterization Study Webinar
DESCRIPTION:Maine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce Waste Characteri
 zation Study Webinar\nMaine Department of Environmental Protection sent th
 is bulletin at 09/09/2026 04:30 PM EDT\n--- PRESS RELEASE ---\nFor Immedia
 te Release\nMaine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce Waste Characteri
 zation Study Webinar\nAUGUSTA\, September 9\, 2026\n— The Maine Departme
 nt of Environmental Protection (DEP) is partnering with the Maine Resource
  Recovery Association (MRRA) and MSW Consultants to provide a live webinar
  and Q&A session presenting the results of the recently completed statewid
 e waste characterization study.  The study\, commissioned by the DEP and 
 funded entirely through the USEPA's Solid Waste Infrastructure for Recycli
 ng (SWIFR) grant program\, provides a detailed analysis on the composition
  of Maine’s waste stream. The full study is available on the\nDepartment
  Reports webpage\n.\nThe webinar will take place on September 15\nth\n\, 2
 026 from 12:00pm to 2:00pm and will include a robust review of the study d
 ata\, methodology\, and key findings.\nThe webinar will provide ample time
  for questions and discussion with the experts at MSW Consultants who cond
 ucted hands-on research and data analysis of Maine’s waste streams and a
 uthored the waste characterization study.\nRegister for the webinar at MRR
 A’s website:\nhttps://mrra.net/event/webinar-maines-waste-characterizati
 on-study/\nFor additional information\, contact\n:\nDavid R. Madore\, Depu
 ty Commissioner\ndavid.madore@maine.gov\nMaine Department of Environmental
  Protection\nManage Subscriber Preferences\n|\nUnsubscribe\n|\nHelp\n|\nCo
 ntact Us\nSTAY CONNECTED:\nhttps://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/
 bulletins/42943a2
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42943a2
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fe3aa8d8ef8abef9@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260910T162200Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 9/10/2026: Judicial Branch to Hold 'Constitut
 ion Day' Student Town Hall on September 17th at the Capital Judicial Cente
 r in Augusta
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nJudicial Branch to Hold 'Constitution Day' Stud
 ent Town Hall on September 17th at the Capital Judicial Center in Augusta\
 nDate:\n9/10/2026\nSupreme Judicial Court Chief Justice Valerie Stanfill a
 nd members of the Supreme Judicial Court will conduct a student-teacher to
 wn hall on Thursday\, September 17\, 2026\, to commemorate the 239th anniv
 ersary of the signing of the U.S. Constitution.\n"The Constitution is the 
 bedrock and framework of American democracy\," said Chief Justice Stanfill
 . "It shapes the everyday lives of young Americans\, including their indiv
 idual rights and freedoms\, now\, and in the future. We hope the student t
 own hall will spark conversation and curiosity about the role and importan
 ce of the Constitution in establishing the U.S. as a nation based on the r
 ule of law."\nClasses and students are invited to attend and participate b
 y Zoom or in person at the Capital Judicial Center in Augusta. Classes wis
 hing to attend in person should RSVP to Julia.Finn@courts.maine.gov by Wed
 nesday\, September 16 at 5:00 p.m.\nConstitution Day Town Hall at the Capi
 tal Judicial Center\nWhen: Thursday\, Sept. 17\, 2026\nTime: 10:00 a.m. - 
 10:55 a.m. (In person and live via a Zoom webinar. Event will be recorded 
 and posted on the Judicial Branch website.)\nLocation: Capital Judicial Ce
 nter\, 1 Court Street\, Augusta\, Maine.\nFormat: Informal student-teacher
  Town Hall\, with Constitution-related questions from students and teacher
 s.\nHow to attend: In person\, RSVP to Julia.Finn@courts.maine.gov by Sept
 ember 16th at 5:00. Educators\, please contact Julia with any questions.\n
 Join by Zoom:\nhttps://courts-maine-gov.zoom.us/j/95934512748\nPasscode: 6
 58994\nSupporting documents\nConstitution Day Student Town Hall\nhttps://w
 ww.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13362262
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13362262
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
